    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|><|channel>thought\n<channel|><|channel>thought\n<channel|><|channel>thought\n<channel|><|channel>thought\n<channel|><|channel>thought\n<channel|>Some of those sound a bit vague though. Like, when people talk about the \"fairness\" part or the \"responsibility\" part, are they usually arguing that the logic itself is flawed, or is it more that they just think it's a bad idea because it'll cause more division? I'm trying to figure out if there are more formal, legalistic arguments being made against it or if it's mostly just people being resistant to change.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
